{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"WBYA (105.5 FM; "The Wolf") is a radio station licensed to Islesboro, Maine, United States.","title":"WBYA"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The station serves the Mid Coast area with a country music format.","title":"WBYA"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The station is owned by Binnie Media, and broadcasts from a transmitter on U.S. 1 south of Northport.","title":"WBYA"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"WKVV (101.7FM) is a radio station licensed to Searsport, Maine, United States.","title":"WKVV"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Established in 1994 as WBYA, the station serves the Bangor area.","title":"WKVV"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The stations is owned by the Educational Media Foundation.","title":"WKVV"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The station carries Educational Media Foundation's K-LOVE Christian music format, simulcasting co-owned WKVZ.","title":"WKVV"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"KIOF-LP (97.9 FM) is a radio station licensed to serve Las Vegas, Nevada.","title":"KIOF-LP"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The station, founded by Gregory LaPorta (current President and CEO) was established in 2010, is owned by Las Vegas Public Radio Inc. and affiliated with Associated Press (AP), T-Mobile, the Las Vegas Tribune (a division of Tribune Media Group), Syndication Networks and VOA News.","title":"KIOF-LP"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Portsonic Communications, LLC is a local community radio investor and management company for Las Vegas Public Radio Inc.","title":"KIOF-LP"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" KIOF-LP is governed under the Local Community Radio Act of 2010 as a new public radio station to the Las Vegas, Nevada valley.","title":"KIOF-LP"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"WHCL-FM (88.7 FM) is an independent, non-profit, and educational college radio station licensed to the Trustees of Hamilton College operating out of Hamilton College in Clinton, New York, USA.","title":"WHCL-FM"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is the only radio station in the town of Clinton.","title":"WH