n coffin in a Budapest art museum.","title":"Péter Halász (actor)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" He died a month after this, at the age of 62.","title":"Péter Halász (actor)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" He had four children: Judith Halasz, Cora Fisher, Gabor Halasz, and David Halasz.","title":"Péter Halász (actor)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Private Peaceful is a 2012 British war drama film directed by Pat O'Connor and starring Jack O'Connell and George MacKay.","title":"Private Peaceful (film)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is based on the 2003 novel of the same name by Michael Morpurgo.","title":"Private Peaceful (film)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The film marks the final performance of Richard Griffiths.","title":"Private Peaceful (film)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Hours Tour was a small-scale promotional concert tour by David Bowie comprising eight live performances and numerous television appearances in support of the album "Hours".","title":"Hours Tour"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" A new guitarist, Page Hamilton, then ex-Helmet founder member, was drafted to replace Reeves Gabrels whose final performance and association with Bowie ended at the VH1 Storytellers performance on 23 August 1999.","title":"Hours Tour"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Rumours of a split were denied by both parties, until a few months later the story changed as the guitarist admitted that he and Bowie had drifted apart.","title":"Hours Tour"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Meet the Navy was a musical revue produced by the Royal Canadian Navy during World War II.","title":"Meet the Navy"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Directed by Hollywood producer Louis Silver and Broadway choreographer Larry Ceballos, the production premiered in a private performance for servicemen on 2 September 1943 at Toronto's Victoria Theatre.","title":"Meet the Navy"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The first performance open to the public was given on the following 4 September.","title":"Meet the Navy"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The pr