{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lilian Sukis (born 29 June 1939, Kaunas) is a Canadian operatic soprano of Lithuanian birth.","title":"Lilian Sukis"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" After earning diplomas from the University of Toronto and McMaster University, she made her professional opera debut in 1964 as Kate Pinkerton in Giacomo Puccini's "Madama Butterfly" with the Canadian Opera Company.","title":"Lilian Sukis"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 1965 she sang the role of Countess Almaviva in Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's "The Marriage of Figaro" at the Stratford Festival.","title":"Lilian Sukis"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" That same year she became a pupil at the Metropolitan Opera Studio and School.","title":"Lilian Sukis"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" She made her debut at the Met in 1967 as Helen Niles in the world premiere of Marvin David Levy's "Mourning Becomes Electra".","title":"Lilian Sukis"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In 1969 she became a member of the Bavarian State Opera where she remained for more than 20 years.","title":"Lilian Sukis"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" She has also appeared as a guest artist with several major opera houses and opera festivals internationally, including the Bayreuth Festival, the Frankfurt Opera, Graz, the Hamburg State Opera, the Salzburg Festival, and the Vienna State Opera among others.","title":"Lilian Sukis"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The National Peace Jubilee was a celebration, organized by Patrick Gilmore in Boston on June 15, 1869.","title":"National Peace Jubilee"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It featured an orchestra and a chorus, as well as numerous soloists.","title":"National Peace Jubilee"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" More than 11,000 performers participated, including the famous violinist Ole Bull as the orchestra's concertmaster, and Carl Zerrahn as director of the choral forces.","title":"National Peace Jubilee"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The Jubilee became the "high-water mark in the influence of the band in American life".","title":"National Peace Jubilee"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Along with the World's Peace Jubilee and International Musical Festival in 1872, it made Gilmore a famous composer and bandmaster.","title":"National Peace Jubilee"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" For the Jubilee, a newly commissioned "Hymn of Peace" was written by Dr. Oliver Wendell Holmes, set to the music from "American Hymn" by Matthais Keller.","title":"National Peace Jubilee"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival is a 12-day festival of South Indian classical music and dance in Cleveland, Ohio, and is held each year around Easter weekend.","title":"Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The festival is a celebration in honor of Tyagaraja, the famous composer of Carnatic music, who composed thousands of devotional compositions, most in Telugu language .","title":"Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The festival began in 1978, and has since grown to become the largest South Indian classical music and dance festival outside of India.","title":"Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The festival draws its audience from all over the United States, as well as from Canada and other parts of the world.","title":"Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Calcutta School of Music established in 1915 by Phillipe Sandre is one of the premier institutions of India, in the field of Western Classical music and Contemporary classical music.","title":"Calcutta School of Music"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was established in the year 1915 by Phillipé Sandré, a musician of considerable calibre, and a contemporary and friend of the famous composer Saint Saëns.","title":"Calcutta School of Music"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It has a wide ranging canvas of musical disciplines covering both Indian and Western music, dance, speech training, elocution, and drama.","title":"Calcutta School of Music"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The School is an important element of the city of Kolkata, providing liberal instruction in musical subjects on one hand, and also arranging orchestral, chamber and solo music training and concerts, as well as music appreciation sessions throughout the year.","title":"Calcutta School of Music"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Many visiting luminaries of the musical world have visited the School throughout its existence.","title":"Calcutta School of Music"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" this include maestros Yehudi Menuhin, Isaac Stern and Mstislav Rostropovich.","title":"Calcutta School of Music"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The great sitar maestro Pandit Ravi Shankar inaugurated the faculty of Indian Music & Dance during the year 1975.","title":"Calcutta School of Music"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Cenk Celebioglu is a Turkish-born composer whose orchestral compositions combine electronic and live instruments.","title":"Cenk Celebioglu"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He aspires to use his music to establish a bridge between east and west.","title":"Cenk Celebioglu"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He attended Berklee College of Music.","title":"Cenk Celebioglu"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Famous composer Fahir Atakoglu, whom he admired since his young age, has offered much encouragement to Cenk, as he is now dedicated to continue his professional career in creating his own unique music and orchestration for film, trailer & media","title":"Cenk Celebioglu"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Husanlal Bhagatram were one of the earliest music directors in Bollywood.","title":"Husnlal Bhagatram"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The team consisted of Husanlal (1910–1968) and Bhagatram (1916–1973).","title":"Husnlal Bhagatram"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" They were popular composers in the 1940s and 1950s.","title":"Husnlal Bhagatram"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It is said that the concept of a duo of music directors began with them.","title":"Husnlal Bhagatram"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Their family name was Batish; their elder brother Amarnath was also a famous composer of film music in 1940s; Shiv Dayal Batish, yet another contemporary, was also related to them.","title":"Husnlal Bhagatram"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The brothers trained famous music directors Shankar (of Shankar Jaikishan), Laxmikant (of Laxmikant -Pyarelal) Khayyam and the singer, Mahendra Kapoor.","title":"Husnlal Bhagatram"}],"peer_messages":[" music and Contemporary classical music.","title":"Calcutta School of Music"}
