{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Cyclic Defrost is an Australian specialist electronic music magazine.","title":"Cyclic Defrost"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was founded and edited by Sebastian Chan, with current editors Bob Baker Fish, Chris Downton and Peter Hollo.","title":"Cyclic Defrost"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It covers independent electronic music, avant-rock, experimental sound art and left field hip hop.","title":"Cyclic Defrost"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Sixtoo was the main project of a Canadian underground hip hop DJ, producer and rapper Vaughn Robert Squire between 1996 and 2007.","title":"Sixtoo"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He has since retired the Sixtoo name pursuing other directions in electronic music, with a large genre shift from experimental hip hop to deeper club sounds of various tempos.","title":"Sixtoo"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He is also known as C.L. S.C.A.R.R., Speakerbruiser Rob, and Prison Garde.","title":"Sixtoo"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Hip hop or hip-hop is a subculture and art movement developed in South Bronx in New York City during the late 1970s.","title":"Hip hop"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" While people unfamiliar with hip hop culture often use the expression "hip hop" to refer exclusively to hip hop music (also called "rap"), Hip hop is characterized by nine distinct elements or expressive realms, of which hip hop music is only four elements (rapping, djaying, beatboxing and breaking).","title":"Hip hop"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Afrika Bambaataa of the hip hop collective Zulu Nation outlined the pillars of hip hop culture, coining the terms: "rapping" (also called MCing or emceeing), a rhythmic vocal rhyming style (orality); DJing (and turntablism), which is making music with record players and DJ mixers (aural/sound and music creation); b-boying/b-girling/breakdancing (movement/dance); and graffiti art, which he called "aerosol writin'", although many say that the graffiti that hip hop adopted had been around years earlier, and had nothing to do with hip hop culture.","title":"Hip hop"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" (visual art).","title":"Hip hop"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Other elements of hip hop subculture and arts movements beyond the main four are: hip hop culture and historical knowledge of the movement (intellectual/philosophical); beatboxing, a percussive vocal style; street entrepreneurship; hip hop language; and hip hop fashion and style, among others.","title":"Hip hop"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Experimental hip hop, also known as abstract hip hop, is a genre of hip hop that employs structural elements typically considered unconventional in traditional hip hop music.","title":"Experimental hip hop"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Some notable experimental hip hop record labels include Definitive Jux, Anticon, Big Dada and Ninja Tune.","title":"Experimental hip hop"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" While most experimental hip hop incorporates turntablism and is produced electronically, some artists have introduced acoustic elements to the music to facilitate it being performed live.","title":"Experimental hip hop"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Beautiful Eulogy is a Christian experimental hip hop group and production team from Portland, Oregon, signed to the label Humble Beast.","title":"Beautiful Eulogy"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Composed of rappers Braille and Odd Thomas and producer Courtland Urbano, the group coalesced in 2011 while the three artists were involved in the creation of Braille's seventh release, "Native Lungs".","title":"Beautiful Eulogy"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Known for its experimental and eclectic sound, the group melds myriad styles of hip hop with genres such as folk, electronic, hymn tunes, and modern worship music.","title":"Beautiful Eulogy"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" After contributing a song to the charity compilation "King Kulture" and making a guest appearance on Lecrae's "Church Clothes", the band released its debut album, "Satellite Kite", on June 19, 2012.","title":"Beautiful Eulogy"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" A second album, "Instruments of Mercy", came out on October 29, 2013.","title":"Beautiful Eulogy"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Called one of the most innovative hip hop groups in Portland, Beautiful Eulogy has met with critical acclaim, with particular praise directed at the group's creative, unconventional sound and deep theological lyrics.","title":"Beautiful Eulogy"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"This is a list of sound artists.","title":"List of sound artists"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Sound art is a diverse group of art practices that considers wide notions of sound, listening and hearing as its predominant focus.","title":"List of sound artists"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" There is contention as to which artists are “sound artists” or if another category might be more accurate such as experimental music, electronic music, sound installation, circuit bending, sound sculpture, builder of experimental musical instruments, noise music, acoustic ecology, sound poetry, installation art, performance art or Fluxus.","title":"List of sound artists"}],"peer_messages":[" music.","title":"Experimental hip hop"}
