ts, decriminalization of illegal drugs on a federal level, a return to the gold standard, the abolition of the Federal Reserve and a reduction in all government spending.","title":"Ron Paul presidential campaign, 1988"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Spider Performance Icebreaker At The Granite is an annual cashspiel, or curling tournament, that takes place at the Granite Curling Club in Winnipeg.","title":"Icebreaker at The Granite"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The Event has been a part of the World Curling Tour since 2017.","title":"Icebreaker at The Granite"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The tournament is held in a round robin format.","title":"Icebreaker at The Granite"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The 2016 event was known as the 2016 Performance Spider Midweek Special and was held in Waterloo, Ontario and was only part of the Ontario Curling Tour.","title":"Icebreaker at The Granite"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The 2016 event included both genders, and in 2017 a separate women's event was added.","title":"Icebreaker at The Granite"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Louisville Zombie Attack started on August 29, 2005 as a flash mob, is a public event in Louisville, Kentucky held annually in August.","title":"Louisville Zombie Attack"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Before 2016, it had been held on August 29 at 8:29 p.m., but the 2016 event was moved to August 27 (which fell on a Saturday that year) at the same time and rebranded as the "Louisville Zombie Walk".","title":"Louisville Zombie Attack"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" This resulted in a lawsuit between two of the event's co-founders, John King and Lyndi Curtis, which resulted in Curtis abandoning all rights to the event.","title":"Louisville Zombie Attack"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The Louisville Zombie Walk's co-organizer, Jason Bessemann, was not named in the suit and went on to promote the 2017 Louisville Zombie Walk as a separate event three days before the original.","title":"Louisville Zombie Attack"},{"sentence_id":4,